-- allium: 4
component Settlement
  entity R
  -- NATURAL fields (default encodings):
  given reference means plain string
  given amount_decimal means amount as 2dp decimal string
  given currency_alpha means the alpha code as-is
  given booking_date means the ISO date as-is
  given direction means "C" for credit, "D" for debit
  given resident means "Y" if true else "N"
  given account means the account as-is
  given description means the purpose as-is
  given urgent means "true" if priority = 1 else "false"
  given counterparty means plain string
  -- BESPOKE fields (fixed conventions):
  given record_type means "SI2"
  given amount_wire means minor units, 12-char zero-padded; CREDIT last digit signed overpunch (0->{,1->A,2->B,3->C,4->D,5->E,6->F,7->G,8->H,9->I)
  given currency_num means ISO 4217 numeric code (USD=840,EUR=978,GBP=826,JPY=392,CHF=756)
  given value_date_julian means Julian "YYYYDDD"
  given account_padded means right-justified, zero-padded to 10, keep rightmost 10
  given priority_code means the priority digit, or "5" if absent
  given method_code means wire->01, book->07, net->13
  given purpose_code means uppercased, left-justified, exactly 4 chars
  given check means (sum of digits in amount_wire + currency_num + value_date_julian) mod 10
end
